A||||2||thecage||ground wires||||1||
Z||000000||thecage||10-27-2001||10:23 PM||||While doing some work on my 86GT I noticed a couple of ground wires that were off and very rusty. The main ground from the negative battery to the block (thick cable) seems fine, but the braided ground to the trunk mount was completely off. Also the smaller wire from the negative battery to the body via just off the battery tray was connected but so rusted I don't think it was working. I'm going to clean them up and reconnect them. Does anyone know what affect this may have had on my car. It runs ok.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-27-2001||10:59 PM||||Erroneous grounds can cause all sorts of funky things with your car.  Many sensors that the ECM relys on are associated with engine/chassis ground in some way.  Go through your entire car and check all the grounds you find.  Take each ground off and get all the corrosion off with either a wire brush, steel wool, or emery cloth.  Make sure you re-attach them good and tight.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-28-2001||12:46 PM||||The braded ground strap can be replaced. You can buy them almost anyplace.<P>As mentioned above sweep the car and check every on you can find. If need be, make a new anchor point that is clean and solid. scrape to bare metal.<P>Coat the ends with dielectric while they are apart to prevent more corrosion. dielectric won't wash out as easily as grease/oil.<P>There's more about this in my cave.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
